WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:11.700
99. Social Contagion. We all understand that certain illnesses are contagious. We

2
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.740
don't share a drink with someone who has a cold. We also wash our hands after we

3
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.060
cough on them to keep from spreading germs. But we're discovering now that

4
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:27.980
germs aren't the only things that are contagious. Ideas and states of being can

5
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.900
be catching too. You must have noticed how you'll probably yawn if your friend

6
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.220
yawns, or if a friend tells you an angry story, you may feel yourself getting

7
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:46.020
angry. One person crying tends to make other people cry. This happens because of

8
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.660
our genes. When we watch someone else feel something or do something, the very

9
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.180
same parts of our brains that would control that emotion or action become

10
00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:02.620
active. Human beings were designed to share each other's feelings and emotions.

11
00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:09.180
Imitating other people's words and behavior is only natural for us. Imagine

12
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.980
that you have an overweight friend. This friend always orders too much food. When

13
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:20.500
you go out with him, you order a lot as well. Can you see how you'd end up

14
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.180
gaining weight that way? That's social contagion. If you have an overweight

15
00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:31.820
spouse or sibling, the chances that you will be overweight increase. Or imagine

16
00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:36.620
drinking and smoking. If your friends do those things, the chances that you will

17
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:42.900
try them increase. Understanding social contagion can help us live happier,

18
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:48.380
healthier lives. If you want to quit smoking, spend time with people who don't

19
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.540
smoke. Recognize when you and your friends are only encouraging each other

20
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:59.100
to complain. Once you know how other people affect you, you can surround

21
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.660
yourself with positive influences.
